description:
Every API endpoint exposed by the system must have a corresponding OpenAPI 3.x schema. Request validation MUST be performed against that schema at the API gateway layer.

This prevents injection attacks, ensures API contract compliance, and provides a machine-readable specification for client SDK generation.

## Examples

### Compliant
```typescript
import { validateRequest } from '@/middleware/validation';
import { createUserSchema } from '@/schemas/users';

export const createUser = validateRequest(createUserSchema)(async (req, res) => {
  // handler logic
});
```

### Non-Compliant
```typescript
export const createUser = async (req, res) => {
  const { name, email } = req.body; // No validation
  // handler logic
};
```
